From b1f59d3aded848c84d6682d55be648e4b071f18d Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ian Blenke <ian@blenke.com>
Date: Sat, 11 Jul 2026 23:36:38 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 06837/11362] ARC round-2 (codex): su15 L3 -> L7 (+4 levels)

Continuation of the same-day breadth-campaign game loop. su15 jumped from
L3 to L7 in a single session, confirming a prior honest partial's own
"untested counter" hypothesis was correct: L4's hunter-evasion wall breaks
via an axis-speed race (the highest-tier fruit outruns the hunter with
axis-aligned 8px hops). L5 introduces hunter-fusion (two hunters converging
into a composite thief) with exact mass accounting; L6 adds a
tier-downgrade/socket mechanic; L7 is a synchronized four-action race to
build and deliver two fruits before the next attack.

Fixed a resolver bug (same class as several this session): su15's new
artifact stores dict-shaped labels, but the priority branch needed the
same JSON-string normalization as bp35/re86/s5i5/sp80. Independently
re-verified per project discipline: 5x fresh env.reset() + replay via the
fixed resolver, all 5 confirmed reached_level=7. L8 was scouted (three
hunters, a genuine simultaneous-control wall) but not won this session.

reproducible_total_levels: 131 -> 135 (verified against a fresh sum). 13 of
18 round-2 games now processed; remaining: lf52, r11l, re86, s5i5.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
