+  - 'L4-L7 SOLVED round 2 (2026-07-11, gpt-5.6-sol via codex, post-wa30 breadth
+    campaign): confirms the "outrun the hunter" hypothesis above was the
+    right unlock -- L4 hunter evasion is an axis-speed race, the highest-tier
+    fruit outruns the 7-colored hunter with repeated 8px axial hops
+    (long axis-aligned hops create separation; diagonal hops often do not),
+    letting a decoy fruit be parked at the far edge while the other half is
+    built. L5 introduces TWO hunters that FUSE into an e-colored composite
+    thief when they converge (the composite hides under a fruit and
+    repeatedly downgrades it); L5''s resource meter is nearly exact so avoid
+    extra failed clicks. L6 adds high tiers c/8 plus a hunter-processing
+    socket: an 8 can be downgraded to c then to the required b via timed
+    collision/withdrawal, with the level transition resolving one tick
+    later. L7 is a synchronized race: four 6-fruits form one b in four
+    actions while the hunter converts 8->c->b in parallel; both b fruits can
+    then be delivered before the next attack (needs two hops for the right
+    b, via (48,24) then (44,22) -- clicking (44,22) directly from spawn is
+    outside pull range and wastes the critical timing window). Independently
+    re-verified by the outer loop: 5x fresh env.reset() + replay via the
+    fixed resolver (labels are dict-shaped, needed JSON normalization), all
+    5 confirmed reached_level=7, state=GameState.NOT_FINISHED. L8 was
+    scouted (three hunters, two c goals, four blobs, an e goal; two hunters
+    fuse on tick 6; careless clicks within radius of both c fruits merge
+    them back into an 8) but not won this session -- a genuine
+    simultaneous-control wall (keeping both c fruits separated and safe
+    while preserving the fused e and avoiding the third hunter).'
   dead_ends:
   - Exp4546 unbounded fruit-relative best-first search from L2 stalled before a gate because fresh-env replay per candidate was too noisy/expensive; the banked route came from reverse-engineering the drag/merge radius and constructive merge staging.
